ing.</article-title><source>Electrophoresis</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>2714</fpage><lpage>2723</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9504803</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Lee1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Vasmatzis</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Stabilization of protein structures.</article-title><source>Curr Opin Biotechnol</source><volume>8(4)</volume><fpage>423</fpage><lpage>428</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9265720</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Shortle1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shortle</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Stites</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name><name><surname>Meeker</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name></person-group><year>1990</year><article-title>Contributions of the Large Hydrophobic Amino Acids to the Stability of Staphylococcal Nuclease.</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><volume>29(35)</volume><fpage>8033</fpage><lpage>8041</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2261461</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Machius1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Machius</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Declererck</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Huber</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wiegand</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>kinetic stabilization of Bacillus Licheniformis alpha-amylase through inroduction of hydrophobic residues at the surface.</article-title><source>J Biol chem</source><volume>278(13)</volume><fpage>11546</fpage><lpage>11553</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12540849</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Xie1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Xie</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Flint</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Vardakou</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lakey</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Probing the Structural Basis for the Difference in Thermostability Displayed by Family 10 Xylanases.</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><volume>360(1)</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>167</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16762367</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-VandenBurg1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van den Burg</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Dijkstra</surname><given-names>BW</given-names></name><name><surname>Vriend</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Der Vinne</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Venema</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>protein stabilization by hydrophobic interactions at the surface.</article-title><source>Eur J Biochem</source><volume>220</volume><fpage>981</fpage><lpage>985</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8143751</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Manning1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Manning</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Colon</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>structural basis of protein kinetic stability: resistance to sodium dodecyl sulfate suggests a central role for rigidity and bias towards beta-sheet structure.</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><volume>43(35)</volume><fpage>11248</fpage><lpage>11254</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15366934</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Mamo1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mamo</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Delgado</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mattiasson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaul</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>clonning, sequencing analysis and expression of a gene encoding an endoxylanase from Bacilus halodurans S7.</article-title><source>Mol Biotechnol</source><volume>33</volume><fpage>149</fpage><lpage>159</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16757802</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Chang1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsai</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsai</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Tseng</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>clonning and characterization of two thermostable xylanases from an alkalophilic Bacillus firmus.</article-title><source>Biochem Biophys Res Commun</source><volume>319(3)</volume><fpage>1017</fpage><lpage>1025</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15184083</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Nakasako1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nakasako</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Large-scale networks of hydration water molecules around bovine beta-trypsin revealed by cryogenic X-ray crystal structure analysis.</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><volume>289(3)</volume><fpage>547</fpage><lpage>564</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10356328</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Goldenberg1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldenberg</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Berget</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1982</year><article-title>Maturation of the tail spike endorhamnosidase of Salmonella phage P22.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>257(13)</volume><fpage>7864</fpage><lpage>7871</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7045114</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Ihsanawati1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ihsanawati</surname><given-names>KT</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaneko</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Morokuma</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Yetsunami</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sato</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Structural basis of the substrate subsite and the highly thermal stability of xylanase 10B from Thermotoga maritima MSB8.</article-title><source>Proteins</source><volume>61(4)</volume><fpage>999</fpage><lpage>1009</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16247799</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Markert1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Markert</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>K&#x000f6;ditz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mansfeld</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Arnold</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Ulbrich-Hofmann</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Increased proteolytic resistance of ribonuclease A by protein engineering.</article-title><source>Protein Eng</source><volume>14(10)</volume><fpage>791</fpage><lpage>796</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11739898</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Bradford1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bradford</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1976</year><article-title>A rapid and sensitive method for the quantitation of microgram quantities of protein utilizing the principle of protein-dye binding.</article-title><source>Anal Biochem</source><volume>72</volume><fpage>248</fpage><lpage>254</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">942051</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003063-Laemmli1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Laemmli</surname><given-names>UK</given-names></name></person-group><year>1970</year><article-title>Cleavage of structural proteins during the assembly of the head of bacteriophage T4.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>227(5259)</volume><fpage>680</fpage><lpage>685</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5432063</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>This work was supported by funds from the International Centre for Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology, New Delhi and the Department of Biotechnology (DBT), Government of India.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>